  abstract = {We report a Monte Carlo study for the transition properties of a classical two-dimensional 1600-electron system. Various structural quantities are calculated. We find a solid phase for 𝛤{$>$}\textasciitilde 1⁢2⁢4, an intermediate phase for 122{$<$}𝛤{$<$}124, and a liquid phase for 𝛤{$<$}\textasciitilde 122. The behavior of both the positional and orientational correlation functions in the three phases is in good agreement with the Kosterlitz-Thouless-Helperin-Nelson-Young theory. The phase transition is continuous, with an intermediate hexatic phase separating the solid and liquid phases.},
